  "summary": "# Health-Tech Daily Digest — June 19, 2026\n\nMedicare Advantage continues to face scrutiny as CMS recalculates star ratings, adding program volatility while bonus payments have surged to $16 billion annually. Meanwhile, Eli Lilly is enforcing compliance by eliminating 340B drug discounts to hospitals failing to provide claims data, signaling pressure on the industry to meet transparency requirements. On the clinical front, an FDA advisory panel endorsed Moderna's mRNA flu vaccine despite earlier controversy, and a new study found that shingles vaccination may reduce dementia risk by 24 percent in nursing home residents. Primary care consolidation is accelerating with Lantern and Marathon Health partnering to integrate primary and specialty care for employers, while Kardigan went public with $400 million in funding for drugs targeting root causes of heart disease. Across the sector, digital maturity and thoughtful AI implementation are emerging as critical differentiators—healthcare leaders are being urged to move beyond aggressive spending toward purposeful transformation that prioritizes physician autonomy and patient trust. Public health concerns also surfaced, including a 40 percent surge in Ebola cases in Congo and Uganda, rising synthetic opioid deaths from nitazenes, and affordability challenges, with only about half of U.S. adults now able to afford quality health care.",
